Apache-2.0. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.

All code in this package is our own (DreamingOfClouds lanes PRICEKIT, TOKDEBT, SEEDBUILD, OWNRETIME, DUALWORD, DUALSCAN,
NETCAUX, REBUILDKIT, NETC4, KFORMULA, CALLEROUT and CALLEROPEN). CALLEROPEN (layout_price.py, cap_check.py) is an
outside-session lane of DreamingOfClouds'. No code from any other pull request or author is included or run;
validate.py and tests/test_checkers.py call the repository's own invoice tools scripts/compare_recursive_invoices.py and
scripts/evaluate_recursive_power.py, pinned in SOURCES.json.

Data, used as data only:
- data/base-7546-word.json.gz is the #7546 word by ToikY (bytes of expected/role902-WORD.json.gz at #7546 head
  99438c43df7aac1e5dbcc43c1578fcd886c119ec, SHA256 pinned in tests/common.py); credit ToikY. #7546 builds on our #7542
  and Clear1nsight's #7334.
- data/caller-7113.json.gz is the signed 17-stage #7113 caller by Rohan Arun in the #7113 caller format (gzip of our
  extracted JSON, content SHA256 pinned in tests/common.py); credit Rohan Arun.
- data/edits-7601.json is our own #7601 edit list.

Credit Clear1nsight, ToikY and the other contributors of the P104 price and replay lineage for the word and invoice
conventions these tools follow. Our earlier toolkit research/p104-designer-toolkit-v2 (#6170) targets the older #6030
word lineage; this package targets the hosted-word format of #7546 and later.
